      "writtenOn": "2026-04-10T14:12:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Android randomizes the MAC address of the device on Wi-Fi even without this option on, it\u0027s a great little privacy feature, that feature just makes it so that it\u0027s random every time, not a random one that stays the same per SSID. Without that randomization, the device is easily trackable between networks\n\n```suggestion\n- [ ] Wi-Fi MAC randomization (make sure MAC address in connection settings doesn\u0027t match the device\u0027s)```",
      "revId": "c7521ade1edde298c31af5ef7398c98123898594",
      "serverId": "35266860-6252-469c-a67d-185064479fc0"
    },
